    "body": "This issue appears to be a duplicate of:\n\n- #48483\n\n**If this is indeed a duplicate:**\nPlease close this issue and subscribe to the linked issue for updates (select \"Close as not planned\" → \"Duplicate\")\n\n**If this is a different issue:**\nNo action needed. A maintainer will review this shortly.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Why were these issues selected?</summary>\n\n**#48483:** Both issues involve Zed failing to work with podman devcontainers on Windows. Issue #48483 shows the exact same error pattern where Zed tries to exec commands on stopped containers without starting them first. The new issue shows similar symptoms with podman not working despite Docker compatibility mode being enabled.\n\n**Shared root cause:** Zed's podman devcontainer implementation fails to properly start stopped containers before attempting to execute commands\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<sub>This is an automated analysis and might be incorrect.</sub>",
