    "body": "> This issue appears to be a duplicate of:\n> \n> * [Zed failing to start podman containers #48483](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/issues/48483)\n> \n> **If this is indeed a duplicate:** Please close this issue and subscribe to the linked issue for updates (select \"Close as not planned\" → \"Duplicate\")\n> \n> **If this is a different issue:** No action needed. A maintainer will review this shortly.\n> \n> Why were these issues selected?\n> **[#48483](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/issues/48483):** Both issues involve Zed failing to work with podman devcontainers on Windows. Issue [#48483](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/issues/48483) shows the exact same error pattern where Zed tries to exec commands on stopped containers without starting them first. The new issue shows similar symptoms with podman not working despite Docker compatibility mode being enabled.\n> \n> **Shared root cause:** Zed's podman devcontainer implementation fails to properly start stopped containers before attempting to execute commands\n> \n> This is an automated analysis and might be incorrect.\n\nThis migh be related, but my issue is not that podman fails to run, but that podman is not used at all... The issue the bot linked is on linux and my issue is on windows.",
