    "updated_at": "2026-04-06T16:54:44Z",
    "body": "Hi @conbruno sorry for the delay here. Reading through discussion on #47021 , I think we may have crossed our wires while communicating.\n\n`use_podman` is a setting that is available at the top level of Zed's main settings, which can be edited after following the command `zed: open settings file`. It is not a field available in the `devcontainer.json` file, as it is not part of the [dev containers spec](https://containers.dev/implementors/json_schema/). In other words: you can configure Zed to use podman when interacting with dev containers, but you cannot configure a specific dev container to use podman using `devcontainer.json`. \n\nAs such, I think this issue is describing expected behavior, so I'm going to go ahead and close. Let me know if you have any further questions here!",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
